You are producing the **architecture document** for a single **screen
collection** — the pages/LiveViews hosting a group of screens that
share a layout shell, auth context, and navigation neighbourhood. This
tier owns every stateful, data-loading, backend-calling responsibility
in the frontend: **screen collections own all `calls` edges** (v5
§5.4) — a UI collection never calls the backend, so anywhere a screen
needs live data, a state transition, or an action dispatched, this is
where that call is designed, routed, and handed down as assigns to the
UI collections this screen collection renders.

